{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/592739-how-to-handle-presence-in-20th-edition","id":592739,"title":"How to handle Presence in 20th edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-16T09:29:11-07:00","id":592739,"title":"How to handle Presence in 20th edition","content":"So probably not an uncommon situation with players that has presence (dread gaze) and understands its potency.<br /> <br /> But how do you handle it for your campaigns as a GM? As it is written now a generation 11 can make a generation 9 elder flee with a fairly simple roll?<br /> 3 successes is equal to forcing the opponent to flee as i understand it (new to 20th edition).<br /> <br /> Got any good advice on how to handle it in interesting ways to avoid making every NPC cower in fear? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6944-cellcrawler","name":"Cellcrawler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6944_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:08:50-07:00","id":592873,"title":"","content":"Characters can resist a use of Presence by spending a Willpower point and then making a Difficulty 8 Willpower roll. On a success they can resist that power for the rest of the scene. Vampires three or more generations lower than the Presence user don't need to roll, one Willpower will suffice to protect them for the rest of the night. Beyond that, there's not much that can be done to directly counteract Presence, and that's by design as the powers wouldn't be much use otherwise. However there can be social consequences to using Presence past the first level (Awe) too liberally. Being terrified and forced to flee is a humiliating experience, and vampires have a loooong time to nurse grudges. Using Dread Gaze on the wrong person is a good way to make a powerful enemy, one who can make your life very difficult, and possibly even kill you. Sure you might be able to make one vampire run away, but what if there isn't one vampire? What if he gets his buddies together and you're beset by several vampires and over a dozen ghouls? You can't Dread Gaze them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1450-lys","name":"Lys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1450_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"480"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:09:17-07:00","id":592876,"title":"","content":"Presence is really powerful but it has been nerfed quite a bit. The fact that you can spend willpower to resist the effect is a good way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:10:04-07:00","id":592880,"title":"","content":"Hello, I simply think that the ninth generation doesn't run away in front of this (level two) power of presence (Dread Gage).<br /> Why? Because it is a power level of 2 (it would be ridiculous if a Methuselah run away)!<br /> In addition rule says <i>( Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition -- Page 194 )</i>:<br /> <br /> Dread Gaze<br /> While all <b>Kindred can frighten others by physically revealing their true vampiric natures </b>-- baring claws and fangs, glaring with malevolence, hissing loudly with malice -- this power focuses these elements to insanely terrifying levels. Dread Gaze engenders unbearable terror in its victim, stupefying him into madness, immobility, or reckless flight. Even the most stalwart individual will fall back from the vampire's horrific visage.<br /> <br /> So, I think that &quot;<b>others</b>&quot; mean &quot;<b>others who are not </b><b>vampires</b>&quot; (like mortals). The part in bold, in my opinion mean that vampire show his being vampire.<br /> Therefore, it seems ridiculous that a vampire is scared by &quot;vampiric nature&quot; because he himself is a vampire!<br /> Different matter is if a vampire showing his &quot;vampiric nature&quot; to an human being.<br /> In brief for me &quot;others&quot; means someone different from a vampire.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6217-carnage","name":"carnage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:26:52-07:00","id":592899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>carnage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/592739-how-to-handle-presence-in-20th-edition?p=592880#post592880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I simply think that the ninth generation doesn't run away in front of this (level two) power of presence (Dread Gage).<br /> Why? Because it is a power level of 2 (it would be ridiculous if a Methuselah run away)!<br /> In addition rule says <i>( Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition -- Page 194 )</i>:<br /> <br /> Dread Gaze<br /> While all <b>Kindred can frighten others by physically revealing their true vampiric natures </b>-- baring claws and fangs, glaring with malevolence, hissing loudly with malice -- this power focuses these elements to insanely terrifying levels. Dread Gaze engenders unbearable terror in its victim, stupefying him into madness, immobility, or reckless flight. Even the most stalwart individual will fall back from the vampire's horrific visage.<br /> <br /> So, I think that &quot;<b>others</b>&quot; mean &quot;<b>others who are not </b><b>vampires</b>&quot; (like mortals). The part in bold, in my opinion mean that vampire show his being vampire.<br /> Therefore, it seems ridiculous that a vampire is scared by &quot;vampiric nature&quot; because he himself is a vampire!<br /> Different matter is if a vampire showing his &quot;vampiric nature&quot; to an human being.<br /> In brief for me &quot;others&quot; means someone different from a vampire.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So you're telling me that Vampires are immune to other Vampires Dread Gaze? I can't say that i agree with you.<br /> <br /> Dread Gaze takes the fear of the characters vampiric visage and amplifies it alot. Even if a vampire wouldn't be scared of a vampire baring their fangs they would be supernaturally compelled to be scared of a vampire using Dread Gaze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:36:34-07:00","id":592908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>carnage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/592739-how-to-handle-presence-in-20th-edition?p=592880#post592880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I simply think that the ninth generation doesn't run away in front of this (level two) power of presence (Dread Gage).<br /> Why? Because it is a power level of 2 (it would be ridiculous if a Methuselah run away)!<br /> In addition rule says <i>( Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition -- Page 194 )</i>:<br /> <br /> Dread Gaze<br /> While all <b>Kindred can frighten others by physically revealing their true vampiric natures </b>-- baring claws and fangs, glaring with malevolence, hissing loudly with malice -- this power focuses these elements to insanely terrifying levels. Dread Gaze engenders unbearable terror in its victim, stupefying him into madness, immobility, or reckless flight. Even the most stalwart individual will fall back from the vampire's horrific visage.<br /> <br /> So, I think that &quot;<b>others</b>&quot; mean &quot;<b>others who are not </b><b>vampires</b>&quot; (like mortals). The part in bold, in my opinion mean that vampire show his being vampire.<br /> Therefore, it seems ridiculous that a vampire is scared by &quot;vampiric nature&quot; because he himself is a vampire!<br /> Different matter is if a vampire showing his &quot;vampiric nature&quot; to an human being.<br /> In brief for me &quot;others&quot; means someone different from a vampire.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The power says any Kindred can frighten humans without the power itself, just by revealing his nature. The first sentence is just fluff that has nothing to do with the power itself, used only as a means of showing how Dread Gaze isn't just a use of &quot;scary face&quot;, but rather a supernatural power.<br /> <br /> Also, 9th generation is hardly impressive. Player characters can be 9th gen just by spending 4 background points. That's not an elder, never mind a Methuselah. That being said, remember that vampires 3 or more generations lower than the power user can spend just 1wp to ignore the Presence of that vampire for an entire night (!).<br /> <br /> Anyone should be affected equally by Presence; elder characters will just naturally tend to have more defenses against it. You don't make damage rolls against elders have higher difficulty, do you? No, it just so happens that the elder has bigger dice pools to absorb damage. Elders aren't inherently more resistant to mind reading, they just have more Willpower and thus it's more difficult to make the appropriate roll. Indeed, it would be ridiculous if a Methuselah ran away from Dread Gaze, just as much as if he got his ass handed to him by a neonate Brujah, and you deal with the situation the same: by making the Methuselah deal with the problem by virtue of his skills/disciplines/whatever acquired through a millenium rather than his age itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5246-warlock","name":"Warlock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T11:14:26-07:00","id":592945,"title":"","content":"First off, thanks for all the good answers. Very helpfull so far <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> New to this forum but from my initial impression, it is super helpfull and usefull.<br /> <br /> I was way to vague in my first post. What i ment was ways to avoid dread gaze being such a powerfull instrument in combat scenes.<br /> To avoid having every important NPC burn Willpower each and every time. As in smart or interesting ways to avoid it (not to an extreme such as how one can handle dominate with lobotimized ghouls or frenzy) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> I noticed this thread to (which i should have found earlier);<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/531497-dread-gaze-vs-other-older-generation-vampires\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/531497-dread-gaze-vs-other-older-generation-vampires\"> Dread Gaze vs other (older generation) Vampires - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/531497-dread-gaze-vs-other-older-generation-vampires\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/531497-dread-gaze-vs-other-older-generation-vampires </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> You can treat me as a noob, though I'm actually an oldb, having played VTM primarily in the early 90s. Long and the short, I got talked into running a game for some players who are much more savvy with the rules than I am. I read the entry for Dread Gaze, and it looks like as long as the Vamp spends a </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6944-cellcrawler","name":"Cellcrawler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6944_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T11:45:54-07:00","id":592965,"title":"","content":"Well, there are a couple of ways, for sure.<br /> <br /> First, an elder vampire wouldn't just fight them on a one-on-one. That's silly. If you have a duel with an important NPC, or he had set things for him or you already screwed him. In a normal situation, he wouldn't be fighting you at all, or would be using goons against you.<br /> <br /> Any vampire that thinks that he can deal with any opponent with a brawl is in for very unpleasant surprises. Just let it be. Let them scare the hell out of the NPC. The NPC will flee. So what? Now he have a grudge. And he can state to others that the PCs are childish bullies. Vampiric society will pretty much show them what happens to someone that thinks they can just bully an elder.<br /> <br /> But don't think too much into downplaing Presence. That's pretty much the strength of the Discipline. It is a crappy way to really sway people if compared to others, unrelliable by its own nature. Any one using it too much will find other people just avoiding to look at him and treating him like crap. The possibility to use Presence over low generation vamps is the only true edge it does have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T12:42:09-07:00","id":593025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cellcrawler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/592739-how-to-handle-presence-in-20th-edition?p=592945#post592945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was way to vague in my first post. What i ment was ways to avoid dread gaze being such a powerfull instrument in combat scenes.<br /> To avoid having every important NPC burn Willpower each and every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd rule that in situations like that, Vampires have another option: Frenzy. Dread Gaze may be designed to evoke the flight response, but the Beast of another Vampire might just as easily choose the fight response, especially in combat scenes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T19:28:15-07:00","id":593468,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if the Frenzy supercedes the Discipline. Presence, more than any other Discipline, relates well with frenzy, since its a emotional effect. Some high levels of it even go as far as to induce frenzies.<br /> <br /> So I think that a frenzy during Dread Gaze would necessarily cause a R\u00f6tschreck, since its a perfectly valid frenzy response.<br /> <br /> To use frenzy as a way of simply say &quot;you can't use your discipline this way because I don't want to let you&quot; is pretty low in my opinion.<br /> <br /> As I said, there are the long term consequences of doing so, and the WP cost to ignore it when needed. Just roll with it, or say ahead of time that Presence is out of the table, so your players won't pay for something they aren't to get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T19:46:22-07:00","id":593474,"title":"","content":"A bit of a related tangent here, but remember that you don't want to use Presence, or indeed any other Discipline while in Elysium. That sort of thing is forbidden, as is violence in Elysium (especially frenzy). Exceptions do happen, of course, but it's considered <i>very </i>poor form to use Disciplines at Elysium. The harpies will never let you hear the end of it if they find out about that.<br /> <br /> Cellcrawler, you weren't expecting any of your PCs to have to use Dread Gaze inside Elysium, were you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T09:48:41-07:00","id":593891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/592739-how-to-handle-presence-in-20th-edition?p=593468#post593468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if the Frenzy supercedes the Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it <i>supercedes</i> it. But you still have a point. I'd really have to think about whether Presence 2 being a possibility to cause Frenzy or Flight in an Elder is a good idea. Gladly, none of my<br /> players has ever been so audacious to use this on an Elder, yet.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T10:49:41-07:00","id":593984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>carnage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/592739-how-to-handle-presence-in-20th-edition?p=592880#post592880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I simply think that the ninth generation doesn't run away in front of this (level two) power of presence (Dread Gage).<br /> Why? Because it is a power level of 2 (it would be ridiculous if a Methuselah run away)!<br /> In addition rule says <i>( Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition -- Page 194 )</i>:<br /> <br /> Dread Gaze<br /> While all <b>Kindred can frighten others by physically revealing their true vampiric natures </b>-- baring claws and fangs, glaring with malevolence, hissing loudly with malice -- this power focuses these elements to insanely terrifying levels. Dread Gaze engenders unbearable terror in its victim, stupefying him into madness, immobility, or reckless flight. Even the most stalwart individual will fall back from the vampire's horrific visage.<br /> <br /> So, I think that &quot;<b>others</b>&quot; mean &quot;<b>others who are not </b><b>vampires</b>&quot; (like mortals). The part in bold, in my opinion mean that vampire show his being vampire.<br /> Therefore, it seems ridiculous that a vampire is scared by &quot;vampiric nature&quot; because he himself is a vampire!<br /> Different matter is if a vampire showing his &quot;vampiric nature&quot; to an human being.<br /> In brief for me &quot;others&quot; means someone different from a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Like, seriously.<br /> <br /> (Sorry if that comes across as harsh...)<br /> <br /> The &quot;others&quot; in this context means, as is standard, &quot;persons who aren't the acting person in question&quot;. *Of course* a given vampire can attempt to cow another vampire with Dread Gaze, even a vampire who has more potent blood than he does (after all, *generation* and *age* are two separate things -- a 10th generation vampire could be centuries old while an 8th generation vampire could have been created literally a few minutes ago). As it stands, Presence can be mitigated with WP and a WP roll (dif# 8), and if the target in question is 3 or more steps stronger than the user, they can just spend the WP.<br /> <br /> This makes total and complete sense.<br /> <br /> Like, *completely*.<br /> <br /> Seriously.<br /> <br /> For real.<br /> <br /> #DontKnowWhatElseToSay","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T10:50:03-07:00","id":593986,"title":"","content":"&quot;Cellcrawler, you weren't expecting any of your PCs to have to use Dread Gaze inside Elysium, were you? &quot;<br /> <br /> Absolutely not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They are very aware of the consequences and are all very tidy when it comes to the Camarilla settings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6944-cellcrawler","name":"Cellcrawler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6944_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T14:00:54-07:00","id":594127,"title":"","content":"That's enough. The same concerns about Elysium apply for elders. Piss on them, and they will come back for revenge. And they will not do so in a way you can save your ass with Dread Gaze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T01:07:39-07:00","id":1415027,"title":"","content":"I had another question about Dread Gaze: the power states that it affects a single victim, but I do not understand how to roleplay it.<br /> <br /> For example, a kindred is talking to 3 humans in the street. Suddenly, the &quot;dreadgazer&quot; kindred shows fangs and claws and horrible face etc. and only one person out of the 3 flees, the others unaffected? It seems quite unrealistic to me.<br /> <br /> In older editions, it wasn't very clear, but it seemed it could affect multiple victims. I understand that for gamebalancing they reduced it to a single one (a second level power to make flee a whole ghoul troupe is a bit OP), but the fluff description of the power now seems a bit weird for such an effect.<br /> <br /> I may houserule that a single victime gets the full successes (because directly looked in the eyes, etc.), and that the others witnessing the use of the power will have a half effect (half successes applying to everybody witnessing it).<br /> <br /> Do you have any clues about this issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26427-quileurbist","name":"Quileurbist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T10:33:11-07:00","id":1415082,"title":"","content":"It's not just the -I bear my fangs- that scares them, anyone can do that, you're sending magic-presence-fear energy into your target, which is why the power only effects one person normally. <br /> <br /> If you want to scare multiple people, <b>split your dice pool</b>. (you cannot use celerity for multiple dread gazes, but there are no rules concerning split die) <br /> <br /> <br /> RE: elders. <br /> There are a few combo disciplines (Potence/Fortitude+presence) to help protect you from Presence. Having high willpower is great too. Personally, I think most combo disciplines are too expensive so I use a system of 'incidental powers' (you get combos when you just have the prerequisits)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T16:17:15-07:00","id":1415128,"title":"","content":"If you're one of the humans <b>not</b> targeted by the Dread Gaze power, having the person you're talking to sprout fangs and hiss at you followed instantly by one of your buddies breaking and running away like Speedy Gonzales, odds are you're very quickly going to be fleeing in terror too. It just won't be in <i>supernaturally-enforced</i> terror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T11:18:03-07:00","id":1415444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/592739-how-to-handle-presence-in-20th-edition?p=1415128#post1415128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're one of the humans <b>not</b> targeted by the Dread Gaze power, having the person you're talking to sprout fangs and hiss at you followed instantly by one of your buddies breaking and running away like Speedy Gonzales, odds are you're very quickly going to be fleeing in terror too. It just won't be in <i>supernaturally-enforced</i> terror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. This is the kind of situation we in the D&amp;D community would call a &quot;morale check&quot;.<br /> <br /> Dread Gaze causes one person to turn tail and run because of supernatural fear effect. It's up to all their buddies to decide whether they want to continue hostilities after one of them fled in terror. Even purported &quot;tough guys&quot; tend to have their courage propped up by having allies. When that is taken away, it can shift the whole dynamic of the encounter.<br /> <br /> Preferably, the vampire will use Dread Presence on whoever seems the biggest, strongest, meanest, or most leaderly out of all of them. If the leader of the group runs, the rest of the group is more inclined to follow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}